Hello Paul,

There is no need to transform the variable in question since it is
fully observed. The transformations are generally for those variables
with missing values. Some may help the data fit the normality
assumption more closely, but the "ordinal" transformation isn't one of
those. It simply controls the actual imputed values and their format.
So, other transformations, such as the logistic, square root and
natural log *do* help the algorithm with the data. We'll try to update
the manual to reflect this distinction.

Thanks,
matt.

